<title>USA: Treasury's Rubin cancels Senate panel appearance.</title>
<headline>Treasury's Rubin cancels Senate panel appearance.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin canceled an appearance before the Senate Budget Committee on Monday because he was ill, the committee said.</p>
<p>Rubin, who had attended a Group of Seven meeting in Berlin on Saturday, had been scheduled to testify on the president's budget at 1400 EST/1900 GMT before the Senate Budget Committee.</p>
<p>He is scheduled to appear before the House Ways and Means Committee Tuesday at 1300 EST/1800 GMT.</p>
</text>
